# Result: 05-runner (telemetry-benchmark)

test_command=sh tests/bench-harness_test.sh
id=runner-01 result=green reason=test_runner_01_help_documents_surface + test_runner_01_refuses_bad_arguments (-h and --help print byte-identical usage (cmp) to stdout with exit 0, naming both modes, every flag, the defaults ("default: 1", 1800, bench/results/bench-<UTC timestamp>.jsonl), and the exit contract ("every repetition produced a record" / "harness-internal"); twelve bad-argument cases -- unknown flag, non-integer/zero repetitions and timeout, unknown dryrun outcome, missing values, stray positionals, and report-mode flag conflicts -- exit non-zero with the usage on stderr and an empty stdout, writing nothing)
id=runner-02 result=green reason=test_runner_02_both_detected + test_runner_02_forcing_bypasses_detection + test_runner_02_nothing_detected_refuses_loudly + test_runner_02_detected_but_unusable_client_is_skipped (with stubs first on PATH and both config dirs present, auto-detection mirrors install.sh's predicate verbatim: claude then opencode x 2 repetitions = 4 records in run order, the dry-run client in none of them, telemetry from the stub's run; --client dryrun runs on a nothing-detected host and on a both-detected host runs ONLY dryrun; --client claude runs only claude; nothing detected with no --client refuses loudly -- stderr names --client, non-zero exit, no JSONL created; a predicate-detected but adapter-unusable claude (config dir, no CLI) is skipped with a visible stderr warning while opencode still completes, and if every detected client is unusable the refusal is identical to nothing-detected)
id=runner-03 result=green reason=test_runner_03_one_record_per_fresh_repetition + test_runner_03_error_and_timeout_reps_do_not_abort_the_loop (three forced dry-run repetitions append exactly three records with repetition counting 1..3 in run order, outcome approved, tokens_input = 100 x repetition and three distinct fixture-repo cwds with each repetition's own repo showing its one declared/one receipted sub-spec -- proving each rep materializes a fresh repo; --dryrun-outcome error completes 2/2 records; --dryrun-outcome timeout --timeout 1 has the deadline kill the client (group-kill, client.timeout marker) and still completes 2/2 with outcome timeout and wall_clock_ms >= 1000; both loops exit 0)
id=runner-04 result=green reason=test_runner_04_default_jsonl_and_end_report + test_runner_04_outcomes_are_data_not_failures + test_runner_04_internal_failures_exit_before_records + test_runner_04_report_mode_launches_no_client_and_writes_nothing (with no --jsonl the runner creates bench/results on demand and writes exactly one bench-<UTC-stamp>.jsonl (collision-safe suffix keeps invocations disjoint) holding the records, prints the aggregate report to stdout at the end without echoing records, and --model reaches every record as model_pinned; runs whose only outcomes are error or timeout still exit 0; the four harness-internal failures -- forced client detected-not-usable, forced client with no adapter (gemini), an unmaterializable fixture, an unwritable results path -- exit non-zero BEFORE any record exists and print no report (writability is probed last, after selection and validation); report mode exits 0, prints the report, launches no client even on a fully-detected host (both tripwire stubs untouched), and leaves its --jsonl and --baseline inputs byte-identical)
id=runner-05 result=green reason=test_runner_05_run_dirs_are_auditable + test_runner_05_run_dirs_disjoint_across_invocations (every repetition leaves bench/results/runs/<stamp>/<client>-r<rep>/ holding request.txt byte-equal to the fixture scenario, client.stdout (this repetition's raw output, distinct cwd per rep), client.stderr, client.exit (0 approved / 3 erroring dryrun), the 13 collect keys in collect.kv, and client.timeout exactly when the deadline fired (present on the killed rep, absent otherwise, including on error reps); each record's run_id = <stamp>-<client>-r<rep> names its own repetition's dir; two separate invocations leave two default result files and two disjoint run-stamp dirs with different run_ids)
id=runner-06 result=green reason=test_runner_06_discovery_is_mechanical + test_runner_06_suite_is_hermetic_by_construction + test_runner_06_full_cli_works_without_any_client_host (the owning suite is found by run_all's mechanical *_test.sh glob and run_all.sh hardcodes no suite name; hermetic by construction -- a static scan shows the runner is invoked at exactly one code site, the env -i bench_cli funnel that carries only HOME and PATH, no network tool appears in the bench/ tree or the suite's code, and no runner-facing suite line references a real credential location; the whole CLI (run + report) succeeds under env -i with an empty host HOME (no client CLIs, no config dirs, no credentials) while auto-detection refuses on that same host)

Notes for later sub-specs (contract surfaces this receipt pins):
- bench_report <results.jsonl> [<baseline.jsonl>] in bench/lib.sh is 06-report's
  seam: the runner calls it both at the end of a run and in report mode, with
  stdout reserved for the report (progress goes to stderr). Replace its body
  behind the same signature; it currently prints the record count plus the
  per-client outcome distribution and, with a baseline, names the file and
  defers comparison statistics to 06-report. --baseline in run mode is
  accepted and forwarded to it.
- Record field order is pinned (13 collect keys in the clients-05 order after
  the run identity block); the JSONL is append-only per repetition, one file
  per invocation by default, and exit status means "every repetition produced
  a record", never "every record approved" -- statistics must not infer
  failure from outcomes.
- Stamp scheme: run_id/stamp = date -u %Y%m%dT%H%M%S%3NZ (fallback seconds)
  with a shared collision suffix keeping the default JSONL name and the
  runs/<stamp> dir disjoint; 06 must not assume the %3N form parsed records
  carry.
- Runtime/cost realities (this session's trims): the deadline floor is
  --timeout 1 (integer >= 1 validated), so the four timeout-deadline tests
  cost ~1.05s each; stage_runner_checkout builds ONE staged template and
  hardlink-clones it (caveat: tests/harness.sh's stage_checkout reuses the
  globals dest and ver -- helper locals in this suite must not collide);
  runner_farm caches the no-client tool farm via side effect (NOT command
  substitution, which loses the global), and FARM_TOOLS must include sh
  because the funnel runs the CLI through sh.
- Suite-runtime honesty: bench suite 48 tests ~25s; at the machine load seen
  this session (load avg 4-6) a clean-HEAD worktree's tests/run_all.sh itself
  measures 63s, so the sub-60s law is currently failing on this machine
  independent of this sub-spec (this change's suite adds ~14s of that; the
  04 receipt measured the full run at 48s on a calmer machine). Re-measure
  run_all at low load and trim the timeout tests further only if the law
  fails there.
- Scenario-id namespace: 05-runner's runner-01..06 ids collide by name with
  the archived optimize-test-suite change's tests/runner_test.sh tags; grep
  for these ids must be scoped to tests/bench-harness_test.sh.
- Full suite green: 18/18 suites, bench suite pass=48 fail=0 skip=0.
